164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 116 0 R
/T (My biological father lived on promises. I'll come this weekend. I'll bring your school supplies. We'll take a trip. I'll buy you clothes. Big, shining words, thrown out over the phone or in passing, the kind that light up a child's chest with hope. And I waited. I would sit and wait for the weekend that never came, for the supplies that never appeared, for the trip that existed only in his mouth. Every broken promise was one more small crack, until I understood something brutal for a child to learn: we didn't matter to him. In time I realized it wasn't even about us. We were merely the instrument. The only thing he truly wanted was to hurt my mother, to wound her through our hope.)
/E (My biological father lived on promises. I'll come this weekend. I'll bring your school supplies. We'll take a trip. I'll buy you clothes. Big, shining words, thrown out over the phone or in passing, the kind that light up a child's chest with hope. And I waited. I would sit and wait for the weekend that never came, for the supplies that never appeared, for the trip that existed only in his mouth. Every broken promise was one more small crack, until I understood something brutal for a child to learn: we didn't matter to him. In time I realized it wasn't even about us. We were merely the instrument. The only thing he truly wanted was to hurt my mother, to wound her through our hope.)
