/Title (Because a young man who lived his life through so much change learned, almost without meaning to, the two most important lessons there are: I learned to fight, and I learned to let go. To fight for what's worth it, and to release what only weighed me down. To honor the blood that chooses to stay, and to let go of the blood that only knew how to wound.)
