/Title (Because while other children played without ever looking over their shoulders, I already understood things meant for grown-ups. I read silences. I could smell a storm before it formed. I learned to study people the way you study the sky, searching for the sign before the strike. I won't dress it up: it hurt. But there, inside that wound, something different was born. My own way of seeing the world. My own ways of surviving.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 400 0 R
/Next 404 0 R
>>
