440 0 obj
<<
/Title (There was no exact moment, no lightning bolt of revelation. It was something slower, quieter: the steady piling-up of small gestures that, added together, ended up shouting a truth I didn't want to accept.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 438 0 R
/Next 442 0 R
>>
endobj
441 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 443 0 R
/Next 439 0 R
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
/Title (My biological father lived on promises. I'll come this weekend. I'll bring your school supplies. We'll take a trip. I'll buy you clothes. Big, shining words, thrown out over the phone or in passing, the kind that light up a child's chest with hope. And I waited. I would sit and wait for the weekend that never came, for the supplies that never appeared, for the trip that existed only in his mouth. Every broken promise was one more small crack, until I understood something brutal for a child to learn: we didn't matter to him. In time I realized it wasn't even about us. We were merely the instrument. The only thing he truly wanted was to hurt my mother, to wound her through our hope.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 440 0 R
/Next 444 0 R
>>
endobj
443 0 obj
<<
/Title (And it did. Not like one of those empty promises I already knew so well. For real.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 445 0 R
/Next 441 0 R
>>
endobj
444 0 obj
<<
/Title (He never managed it. She was stronger than all his lies combined.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 442 0 R
/Next 446 0 R
>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Title (Little by little, I began to build bridges. One friend, then another. New goals. Purposes I wouldn't have dared to dream of before. And in time we understood something that gave meaning to all the uprooting: moving there was going to make our lives better.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 447 0 R
/Next 443 0 R
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 444 0 R
/Next 448 0 R
>>
endobj
447 0 obj
<<
/Title (But something had changed in me without my noticing. That boy who trembled at every sound had learned, through sheer survival, to observe before he feared. And this time, for the first time, the observing found no danger. It found opportunity.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 449 0 R
/Next 445 0 R
>>
endobj
